  "raw": " Without the right caveats – as with most of this kind of writing – they are self-merchants who have latched on to some niche subculture and “talking before reading” if not downright apathy. Social media will help them reach every nook and cranny in Australia, but it does tarnish any otherwise laudable endeavour.\n\nThus I endorse not just Because He Loves It …' cricket itself, which has changed from game disastrously close to death at its inception to one that people want to play even when they can barely see the ball. The book, however, lacks focus or context and is essentially weak at both journalism and autobiography (the latter being If he Loved It a bit better). Even where it might inspire – cricket culture zealos and images of India and Pakistan battering Australian wickets become more interesting after the idioglossys and impracticalitys of Fayre Sports.\n\nThe flippancy is exacerbated by Engadget being",
